### T-ADM-30 status that is not published/closed: 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/scholarships/{{id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer test-admin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "draft" }

### T-ADM-31 close a draft: 409
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/scholarships/{{id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer test-admin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "closed" }

### T-ADM-32 publish a draft whose deadline has passed: 409 (use a draft made by T-ADM-22)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/scholarships/{{id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer test-admin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "published" }

### T-ADM-33 publish a valid draft: 200 published
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/scholarships/{{id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer test-admin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "published" }

### T-ADM-34 publish it again: 409 Only a draft can be published
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/scholarships/{{id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer test-admin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "published" }

### T-ADM-35 edit after publishing: 409 locked after publishing
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/scholarships/{{id}}
Authorization: Bearer test-admin
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Edited after publish", "description": "For students building on the cloud.",
  "deadline": "2027-01-15T23:59:00Z", "awards": 3,
  "rubric": [
    { "criterionId": "academic", "name": "Academic record", "description": "Grades and transcript", "weight": 50 },
    { "criterionId": "essay", "name": "Essay", "description": "Clarity and motivation", "weight": 50 }
  ],
  "eligibility": { "allowedDomains": ["example-university.edu"], "minGpa": 3, "years": [2, 3] }
}

### T-ADM-36 close a published scholarship: 200 closed (again, or publish, or PUT afterwards: 409)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/scholarships/{{id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer test-admin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "closed" }

### T-ADM-37 five publishes at the same time: exactly one 200 — needs parallel requests, so only in tests/api-tests.sh

### T-ADM-38 publish a corrupt or legacy record (awards 0, or weights not summing to 100): 409, nothing changes.
# The API never stores such a record, so the runner writes it straight into DynamoDB, tries the publish, and deletes it:
# only in tests/api-tests.sh
